\title{A Type Theory with a Tiny Object}
\author{mitchellriley}
\taxon{Reference}
\date{2024-03-04}
\meta{arxiv}{2403.01939}

\subtree{
\taxon{Abstract}
\p{
We present an extension of Martin-Lof Type Theory that contains a tiny object; a type
for which there is a right adjoint to the formation of function types as well as the
expected left adjoint. We demonstrate the practicality of this type theory by proving
various properties related to tininess internally and suggest a few potential
applications.
}
}

